WEBVTT

00:00:01.612 --> 00:00:02.742
After what?

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:06.294
At the beach.

00:00:06.354 --> 00:00:09.726
Hi Kyle.

00:00:09.786 --> 00:00:10.616
How are you?

00:00:10.636 --> 00:00:11.677
Hi Jody.

00:00:11.737 --> 00:00:12.157
Fine.

00:00:12.217 --> 00:00:13.237
Thanks you.

00:00:13.297 --> 00:00:14.598
I'm fine too.

00:00:14.658 --> 00:00:15.538
Thanks.

00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:16.669
Hey.

00:00:16.729 --> 00:00:18.020
What's this?

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:19.810
It's a tracker.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.641
What's it for?

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:22.942
Listen.

00:00:23.002 --> 00:00:24.282
What is it?

00:00:24.342 --> 00:00:25.793
I don't know.

00:00:25.854 --> 00:00:27.785
Wait a minute.

00:00:27.845 --> 00:00:29.396
What's that?

00:00:29.456 --> 00:00:30.978
Oh, it's a can.

00:00:31.038 --> 00:00:33.019
An orange juice can.

00:00:33.079 --> 00:00:34.860
Oh, Kyle, listen.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.792
There's something else here.

00:00:36.852 --> 00:00:37.792
Jody.

00:00:37.852 --> 00:00:38.773
Jody, look.

00:00:38.833 --> 00:00:39.444
Look.

00:00:39.504 --> 00:00:41.354
What are they, Kyle?

00:00:41.414 --> 00:00:46.178
I don't know.

00:00:46.238 --> 00:00:50.942
Chapter Two.

00:00:51.002 --> 00:00:54.930
An exciting discovery.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.998
Are they coins?

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.168
Maybe.

00:00:59.228 --> 00:01:00.899
Look at the writing.

00:01:00.959 --> 00:01:02.409
Is it Spanish?

00:01:02.469 --> 00:01:03.299
I don't know.

00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:05.020
Let's ask my grandpa.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.360
Good idea.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.720
These coins are interesting.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.441
They look very old.

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:12.711
Do you think they're valuable?

00:01:12.771 --> 00:01:14.031
Maybe.

00:01:14.091 --> 00:01:15.201
Excuse me.

00:01:15.242 --> 00:01:16.522
What's in your hand?

00:01:16.582 --> 00:01:17.382
Some coins.

00:01:17.442 --> 00:01:18.572
Have a look.

00:01:18.632 --> 00:01:20.082
Are they silver?

00:01:20.142 --> 00:01:20.933
I don't know.

00:01:20.993 --> 00:01:23.065
We're going to ask my grandfather.

00:01:23.125 --> 00:01:25.069
Come on Kyle, let's go!

00:01:25.089 --> 00:01:28.962
Hey kids, do you want a drink?

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:32.076
Colour, orange juice, chocolate milk?

00:01:32.136 --> 00:01:38.212
Yes please, can we have some orange juice?

00:01:38.272 --> 00:01:51.099
Chapter 3 An accident on the beach How much is that?

00:01:51.159 --> 00:01:52.200
$1.25.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:53.361
Here you are.

00:01:53.421 --> 00:01:57.463
Thank you.

00:01:57.523 --> 00:01:58.874
Watch out!

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:00.555
Are you okay?

00:02:00.615 --> 00:02:01.616
My drinks!

00:02:01.676 --> 00:02:02.737
My drinks!

00:02:02.797 --> 00:02:04.788
Don't worry, they're all right.

00:02:04.848 --> 00:02:06.689
Thanks very much, kids.

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:07.630
That's okay.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:08.971
You're welcome.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:11.573
Oh, Jody, I'm very excited.

00:02:11.632 --> 00:02:14.094
I think the coins are valuable.

00:02:14.154 --> 00:02:16.806
Yes, maybe they are silver.

00:02:16.866 --> 00:02:22.161
Let's go see your grandpa.

00:02:22.221 --> 00:02:32.639
Chapter 4 Are the coins valuable?

00:02:32.699 --> 00:02:37.122
I have the coins!

00:02:37.182 --> 00:02:38.453
What coins?

00:02:38.512 --> 00:02:39.833
What do you mean, buff?

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:40.514
Look!

00:02:40.574 --> 00:02:41.534
Come on!

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.666
Let's take them to my friend Woody!

00:02:43.725 --> 00:02:45.627
What do you think, Woody?

00:02:45.687 --> 00:02:47.228
Are they valuable?

00:02:47.288 --> 00:02:49.399
How many coins do you have?

00:02:49.459 --> 00:02:50.000
Six.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.350
There are six coins.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.360
Hmm...

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.950
These coins are silver.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.722
And they're old.

00:02:58.782 --> 00:03:00.933
They're worth a lot of money.

00:03:00.993 --> 00:03:02.954
How much money, Woody?

00:03:03.014 --> 00:03:05.706
About a million dollars.

00:03:05.766 --> 00:03:08.117
A million dollars!

00:03:08.177 --> 00:03:09.498
Wow!

00:03:09.558 --> 00:03:11.340
Thanks, Woody.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.341
Where are we going, boss?

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.452
To see the museum director.

00:03:15.512 --> 00:03:18.304
Now, don't say another word.

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.642
Here they are, sir.

00:03:20.702 --> 00:03:22.480
These are wonderful.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:23.880
They're very old.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:25.221
Look at the writing.

00:03:25.281 --> 00:03:27.081
They're Spanish.

00:03:27.141 --> 00:03:28.701
What else?

00:03:28.761 --> 00:03:33.272
Look, there's a Spanish ship on the Mandate.

00:03:33.292 --> 00:03:34.582
1662.

00:03:34.642 --> 00:03:37.133
You want the coins for your museum?

00:03:37.193 --> 00:03:37.993
Oh, yes.

00:03:38.053 --> 00:03:39.533
They're very important.

00:03:39.593 --> 00:03:44.414
Let's talk about the money.

00:03:44.474 --> 00:03:53.393
Chapter 5 The coins are missing.

00:03:53.453 --> 00:03:56.355
Grandpa!

00:03:56.415 --> 00:03:57.215
Grandpa!

00:03:57.275 --> 00:03:58.336
Where are you?

00:03:58.396 --> 00:04:00.708
Hi Kyle, I'm in the kitchen.

00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:03.459
We have something for you to look at.

00:04:03.518 --> 00:04:05.270
You look excited.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:06.520
Is it important?

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.662
It's something we found on the beach.

00:04:08.722 --> 00:04:11.684
Well, let's put it on the living room table.

00:04:11.743 --> 00:04:13.404
Oh no!

00:04:13.464 --> 00:04:14.745
Where are they?

00:04:14.805 --> 00:04:16.164
What's the matter?

00:04:16.224 --> 00:04:17.423
My coins!

00:04:17.463 --> 00:04:18.444
They're gone!

00:04:18.503 --> 00:04:19.764
Are you sure?

00:04:19.824 --> 00:04:21.656
Look in your bag again!

00:04:21.716 --> 00:04:24.419
They aren't here, Jody!

00:04:24.479 --> 00:04:26.100
Calm yourself, Kyle.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.442
Try to remember where you put them.

00:04:28.502 --> 00:04:31.355
Do you want the coins, Mr. Thomas?

00:04:31.414 --> 00:04:32.676
Yes, I do.

00:04:32.736 --> 00:04:34.528
How much do you want for them?

00:04:34.588 --> 00:04:37.210
I want a million dollars.

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:39.131
A million dollars?

00:04:39.191 --> 00:04:40.893
We don't have that kind of money.

00:04:40.953 --> 00:04:43.902
A million dollars or no deal?

00:04:43.962 --> 00:04:46.001
Okay, I can try.

00:04:46.061 --> 00:04:47.994
Come back tomorrow afternoon.

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:56.354
If you want these coins, make sure you have the money by 2.30 tomorrow.

00:04:56.414 --> 00:05:08.728
Chapter 6 At the Police Station We were on the beach.

00:05:08.787 --> 00:05:12.028
I put the coins in my bag.

00:05:12.088 --> 00:05:13.289
That's right.

00:05:13.349 --> 00:05:18.040
And then there were those two men with the drinks.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.951
That's it, Jody.

00:05:20.011 --> 00:05:21.792
They were near my bag.

00:05:21.852 --> 00:05:23.862
They have my coins.

00:05:23.922 --> 00:05:24.973
Are you sure?

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.643
Yes, I'm sure.

00:05:26.703 --> 00:05:28.444
Let's go to the police.

00:05:28.504 --> 00:05:30.134
Come on.

00:05:30.194 --> 00:05:32.531
Can you describe the men?

00:05:32.591 --> 00:05:36.830
Yes, one man is tall and thin.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:40.112
He has brown hair and a beard.

00:05:40.172 --> 00:05:41.664
What's he wearing?

00:05:41.724 --> 00:05:45.316
A colored shirt and dark trousers.

00:05:45.376 --> 00:05:47.528
And he's wearing Jim's shoes.

00:05:47.588 --> 00:05:49.209
What about the other man?

00:05:49.269 --> 00:05:51.891
He's short and quite fat.

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:55.144
He has blonde hair and blue eyes.

00:05:55.203 --> 00:05:59.476
He's wearing black boots, blue jeans and a white shirt.

00:05:59.536 --> 00:06:01.414
Can you see the two men?

00:06:01.474 --> 00:06:03.520
No, I can't.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:05.511
Their pictures aren't here.

00:06:05.571 --> 00:06:10.314
I'm sorry, we can't help you.

00:06:10.374 --> 00:06:14.656
Chapter 7.

00:06:14.716 --> 00:06:19.068
Add the coffee shop in the mall.

00:06:19.128 --> 00:06:22.360
A million dollars.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.391
That's a lot of money, boss.

00:06:24.451 --> 00:06:26.601
What are you going to buy?

00:06:26.661 --> 00:06:31.021
Oh, a big house with a swimming pool.

00:06:31.081 --> 00:06:35.162
I want a private jet and some expensive clothes.

00:06:35.222 --> 00:06:39.422
And I want a big boat to sail around the world.

00:06:39.482 --> 00:06:41.263
What time is it?

00:06:41.323 --> 00:06:42.443
12 o'clock.

00:06:42.503 --> 00:06:43.253
Why?

00:06:43.313 --> 00:06:44.454
I'm hungry.

00:06:44.513 --> 00:06:46.314
Let's go eat something.

00:06:46.374 --> 00:06:47.694
Me too.

00:06:47.754 --> 00:06:50.065
Let's go to the coffee shop in the mall.

00:06:50.125 --> 00:06:51.035
Good idea.

00:06:51.095 --> 00:06:52.386
Come on.

00:06:52.446 --> 00:06:54.349
What would you like?

00:06:54.409 --> 00:06:57.050
We want two submarine sandwiches, please.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:07:02.855
And an orange juice for me and chocolate milk for her, please.

00:07:02.914 --> 00:07:07.168
Kyle, there are the two men from the beach.

00:07:07.228 --> 00:07:08.128
Yikes!

00:07:08.188 --> 00:07:10.000
Jody, you're right!

00:07:10.059 --> 00:07:12.371
Where are we going now, boss?

00:07:12.431 --> 00:07:15.283
Oh, I want to think.

00:07:15.343 --> 00:07:16.574
Quick, Jody.

00:07:16.634 --> 00:07:17.695
They're leaving.

00:07:17.755 --> 00:07:19.376
Let's follow them.

00:07:19.436 --> 00:07:20.927
Get back, Jody.

00:07:20.987 --> 00:07:25.548
They mustn't see us.

00:07:25.608 --> 00:07:29.628
Chapter 8.

00:07:29.688 --> 00:07:35.021
Tallman catches Kyle and Jodie.

00:07:35.081 --> 00:07:38.814
Kyle, I can see them.

00:07:38.874 --> 00:07:40.425
They're inside.

00:07:40.445 --> 00:07:42.287
Be careful, Jodie.

00:07:42.346 --> 00:07:45.078
Don't let them see us.

00:07:45.138 --> 00:07:48.210
Boss, listen.

00:07:48.270 --> 00:07:50.703
There's someone outside.

00:07:50.762 --> 00:07:52.334
Are you sure?

00:07:52.394 --> 00:07:53.815
I can't hear anything.

00:07:53.835 --> 00:07:55.658
Yeah, I heard the noise.

00:07:55.718 --> 00:07:57.320
Put me down!

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:59.452
Get your hands off me!

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:01.744
Well, well.

00:08:01.804 --> 00:08:03.806
The kids from the beach.

00:08:03.866 --> 00:08:05.367
What do you want?

00:08:05.427 --> 00:08:07.168
I want my coins.

00:08:07.228 --> 00:08:08.429
Coins.

00:08:08.489 --> 00:08:10.240
What coins?

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:12.052
Put them in the basement.

00:08:12.112 --> 00:08:13.874
We don't want any trouble.

00:08:13.934 --> 00:08:15.656
And tie them up.

00:08:15.715 --> 00:08:18.758
You can shout for help if you want.

00:08:18.818 --> 00:08:22.690
But no one can hear you down here.

00:08:22.749 --> 00:08:25.089
Creep!

00:08:25.149 --> 00:08:27.720
What can we do?

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:29.742
I have an idea.

00:08:29.802 --> 00:08:33.345
There's a pen knife in my pocket.

00:08:33.404 --> 00:08:35.416
Can you get it?

00:08:35.476 --> 00:08:37.557
I can try.

00:08:37.617 --> 00:08:39.999
Can you move nearer, Jody?

00:08:40.058 --> 00:08:41.370
Okay.

00:08:41.429 --> 00:08:46.062
Now try.

00:08:46.123 --> 00:08:50.896
Chapter 9.

00:08:50.956 --> 00:08:54.654
Locked in the basement.

00:08:54.714 --> 00:08:57.223
Good afternoon.

00:08:57.283 --> 00:08:58.384
Please sit down.

00:08:58.444 --> 00:08:59.956
Now, about the coins.

00:08:59.976 --> 00:09:01.408
Do you have our money?

00:09:01.468 --> 00:09:05.272
The museum wants the coins, but we don't have enough money.

00:09:05.332 --> 00:09:06.312
Why not?

00:09:06.372 --> 00:09:08.064
I need more time.

00:09:08.124 --> 00:09:10.527
Can you come back tomorrow?

00:09:10.587 --> 00:09:12.780
I can't get it.

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:14.411
It's too difficult.

00:09:14.431 --> 00:09:17.328
Try it again, Kyle.

00:09:17.388 --> 00:09:19.895
Jody, I have the knife.

00:09:19.955 --> 00:09:21.476
Well done, Kyle.

00:09:21.536 --> 00:09:23.758
Now, cut the rope.

00:09:23.818 --> 00:09:25.889
I can't do it.

00:09:25.949 --> 00:09:27.670
The rope is too thick.

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:29.441
The knife isn't sharp enough.

00:09:29.501 --> 00:09:31.452
Press harder.

00:09:31.512 --> 00:09:33.864
That's it?

00:09:33.924 --> 00:09:35.195
We're free.

00:09:35.255 --> 00:09:37.326
We must try to escape.

00:09:37.386 --> 00:09:39.338
Come on.

00:09:39.398 --> 00:09:41.529
Oh, no.

00:09:41.589 --> 00:09:42.930
We can't get out.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:43.560
Why?

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:44.631
What's the matter?

00:09:44.691 --> 00:09:46.437
The door is locked.

00:09:46.497 --> 00:09:48.322
Can we do now?

00:09:48.382 --> 00:09:50.634
We have to pick the lock.

00:09:50.694 --> 00:09:53.684
We need something small.

00:09:53.744 --> 00:09:55.755
What about this coat hanger?

00:09:55.815 --> 00:09:57.956
No, it's too big.

00:09:58.016 --> 00:09:59.106
Wait.

00:09:59.166 --> 00:10:04.418
Maybe I can use my hair slide.

00:10:04.478 --> 00:10:09.260
Chapter 10.

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:13.092
Kyle and Jody Escape.

00:10:13.152 --> 00:10:15.852
We can't wait.

00:10:15.912 --> 00:10:19.044
We're going to take the coins to another museum.

00:10:19.104 --> 00:10:22.836
No, no, we want those coins for our museum.

00:10:22.896 --> 00:10:25.138
Okay, come back in one hour.

00:10:25.199 --> 00:10:26.520
I will have the money.

00:10:26.579 --> 00:10:28.692
You have one hour.

00:10:28.752 --> 00:10:29.882
Hello?

00:10:29.942 --> 00:10:31.674
I want the police.

00:10:31.734 --> 00:10:33.996
What are you going to do with that?

00:10:34.056 --> 00:10:35.107
Watch.

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:37.319
Put it in the lock.

00:10:37.379 --> 00:10:38.830
Turn it.

00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:41.302
Yes, it's opening!

00:10:41.362 --> 00:10:43.741
I can hear something.

00:10:43.801 --> 00:10:47.470
Boss, I can hear a strange noise.

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:49.132
Maybe it's those kids.

00:10:49.192 --> 00:10:50.112
Go look.

00:10:50.172 --> 00:10:51.793
Stupid kids.

00:10:51.853 --> 00:10:53.694
They can't escape.

00:10:53.754 --> 00:10:56.286
I have the key.

00:10:56.346 --> 00:10:59.088
Shut up you kids.

00:10:59.148 --> 00:11:01.010
Don't make a noise.

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:03.702
You can't escape from here.

00:11:03.762 --> 00:11:06.033
Yes, don't worry sir.

00:11:06.093 --> 00:11:07.684
We'll be good.

00:11:07.744 --> 00:11:10.806
Look at these kinds, tall man.

00:11:10.866 --> 00:11:12.731
Are they real?

00:11:12.791 --> 00:11:15.206
You know they are, boss.

00:11:15.266 --> 00:11:18.258
Mr. Thomas told us that.

00:11:18.318 --> 00:11:19.398
No.

00:11:19.458 --> 00:11:20.700
They're fake.

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:23.211
But they look like the real coins.

00:11:23.271 --> 00:11:26.384
But why do you have fake coins?

00:11:26.444 --> 00:11:28.104
Woody gave them to me.

00:11:28.164 --> 00:11:33.088
I need them for my plan.

00:11:33.148 --> 00:11:45.018
Chapter 11 Shortman's Plan What's your plan, boss?

00:11:45.078 --> 00:11:48.400
I'm gonna sell these fake coins to the museum.

00:11:48.460 --> 00:11:50.752
What are they saying, Kyle?

00:11:50.812 --> 00:11:54.854
They're taking some fake coins to the museum.

00:11:54.914 --> 00:11:58.607
But, boss, where are the real coins?

00:11:58.647 --> 00:12:02.369
They're here in a safe place in the house.

00:12:02.429 --> 00:12:05.931
What are we going to do after we get the money?

00:12:05.991 --> 00:12:09.584
We're gonna take the real coins and leave town.

00:12:09.644 --> 00:12:12.118
Here are our tickets to Mexico.

00:12:12.178 --> 00:12:14.742
Now, let's go.

00:12:14.802 --> 00:12:16.633
It's okay, Jody.

00:12:16.693 --> 00:12:17.694
They're gone.

00:12:17.754 --> 00:12:19.534
Let's call the police.

00:12:19.594 --> 00:12:21.896
No, the coins first.

00:12:21.956 --> 00:12:23.456
I have an idea.

00:12:23.516 --> 00:12:26.748
Let's go get the tracker.

00:12:26.808 --> 00:12:29.459
Try the living room again.

00:12:29.519 --> 00:12:30.470
Nothing.

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:31.720
They're not here.

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:34.112
Let's look in the bedroom.

00:12:34.172 --> 00:12:38.274
What about under the bed or behind the cupboard?

00:12:38.334 --> 00:12:41.796
They're here, near the chest of drawers.

00:12:41.856 --> 00:12:44.467
I think I know where they are.

00:12:44.527 --> 00:12:46.688
They're in the piggy bank.

00:12:46.748 --> 00:12:49.629
The Silver Coins.

00:12:49.689 --> 00:12:51.990
Do you have the money?

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:54.000
Yes, here's your money.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:55.861
Sign your name here.

00:12:55.921 --> 00:12:58.212
Here are the Silver Coins.

00:12:58.272 --> 00:13:02.234
Let's go.

00:13:02.294 --> 00:13:09.906
Chapter 12.

00:13:09.966 --> 00:13:14.817
Boss!

00:13:14.877 --> 00:13:15.977
The kids!

00:13:16.037 --> 00:13:17.338
They're in here!

00:13:17.398 --> 00:13:18.468
They have the coins!

00:13:18.528 --> 00:13:19.018
Quick!

00:13:19.078 --> 00:13:19.988
Get them!

00:13:20.048 --> 00:13:20.998
Jody!

00:13:21.058 --> 00:13:22.819
Run to the basement door!

00:13:22.879 --> 00:13:25.750
Over here, you big gorilla!

00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:27.730
Got you!

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:29.070
Good work, Kyle!

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:30.730
Give me those coins, boy!

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:31.260
Never!

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:32.631
They're my coins!

00:13:32.691 --> 00:13:33.711
This way, Kyle!

00:13:33.771 --> 00:13:34.871
Hurry!

00:13:34.931 --> 00:13:36.521
Help me!

00:13:36.581 --> 00:13:37.662
Help!

00:13:37.722 --> 00:13:39.904
Help!

00:13:39.964 --> 00:13:43.006
Let the boy go, now!

00:13:43.066 --> 00:13:44.516
You are under arrest.

00:13:44.576 --> 00:13:46.468
We're taking you to the police station.

00:13:46.528 --> 00:13:47.648
Okay.

00:13:47.708 --> 00:13:48.979
Okay, guys.

00:13:48.999 --> 00:13:53.320
He's not hurt.

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:58.503
Chapter 13.

00:13:58.563 --> 00:14:02.415
A happy ending.

00:14:02.475 --> 00:14:07.814
You two are going to prison for a very long time.

00:14:07.874 --> 00:14:09.770
I was pesky kids.

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:12.601
Are we going to Mexico now, boss?

00:14:12.661 --> 00:14:15.782
Look Kyle, you and Jody are famous.

00:14:15.842 --> 00:14:17.852
Your story is in the newspaper.

00:14:17.912 --> 00:14:19.052
Let me see.

00:14:19.112 --> 00:14:21.873
Look Jody, there's a photo too.

00:14:21.933 --> 00:14:26.474
Thanks to you Kyle and Jody, those two crooks are locked up in prison.

00:14:26.534 --> 00:14:29.884
And these important coins are safe in the museum.

00:14:29.944 --> 00:14:33.792
Can you tell us something about the coins, Mr. Thomas?

00:14:33.852 --> 00:14:36.701
They are very old and rare coins.

00:14:36.761 --> 00:14:39.092
They come from a Spanish ship.

00:14:39.152 --> 00:14:41.674
Its name was the Atacha.

00:14:41.734 --> 00:14:47.866
In the autumn of 1662, on the 4th of September, it left Cuba for Spain.

00:14:47.926 --> 00:14:50.728
There were a lot of precious things on the ship.

00:14:50.788 --> 00:14:56.690
There were 400 bars of gold and 120,000 silver coins.

00:14:56.750 --> 00:15:01.421
There were pearl necklaces and bracelets, rings and gold plates.

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:04.661
But the weather was bad and the ship was in trouble.

00:15:04.721 --> 00:15:09.696
It sank to the bottom of the ocean and all the precious things were lost.

00:15:09.756 --> 00:15:15.722
The legend says that the ship is still there, under the sea near the Florida coast.

00:15:15.782 --> 00:15:22.326
Sometimes silver coins are found on the beaches near the ship, washed up by the waves.

00:15:22.386 --> 00:15:25.544
What are you going to do with the reward money Kyle?

00:15:25.604 --> 00:15:27.954
I'm gonna buy a bigger tracker.

00:15:28.014 --> 00:15:29.344
Are you crazy?

00:15:29.404 --> 00:15:30.304
Why?

00:15:30.364 --> 00:15:34.305
There were 120,000 coins on the Atocha.

00:15:34.365 --> 00:15:36.846
We found six.

00:15:36.866 --> 00:15:40.046
I want to find the other 119,994.

00:15:40.106 --> 00:15:43.157
Do you want to help me?

00:15:43.217 --> 00:15:44.447
No thanks.

00:15:44.507 --> 00:15:46.077
It's too dangerous.

00:15:46.137 --> 00:15:48.658
I'm going to play beach volleyball.

00:15:48.718 --> 00:15:49.588
It's safer.

